# structgen arguments for sdk/ts/gen/msg_layout.bots.ts: the replay code's
# extras (replay_extras.h ReplayExtras) - the nicknames and per-move timing
# behind the dash in a share link - which the bridge crosses with in both
# directions. Not the codec's own packed blob: that is a C format, packed and
# unpacked beside it (replay_extras_pack). A snapshot reader and a writer, plain
# objects copied out of and back into the module, and the codec's constants, so
# no bridge restates a cap or a number. Read by tools/structgen/gen.sh with
# --cwd c/ and the bots build's flags. The root is in game_layout.args too, so
# the layout hash web.wasm is checked against at load covers these readers.
#
# The browser reaches this module (it reads share links), which is why it is not
# in game_layout.bots.ts - that one holds accessors over the unmasked Game and
# e2e/security_client_boundary keeps it out of the bundle.
#
# The iMessage envelope's header (msg_wire.h MsgHeader) used to be here too. No
# TS reads an envelope any more (the /m/ unfurl is C, in c_base), so the kernel's
# links stopped exporting the decode and the reader went with it.
--header replay_extras.h --root ReplayExtras --snapshot ReplayExtras --writer ReplayExtras
--count ReplayExtras.names=n_names --count ReplayExtras.gaps=n_gaps --count ReplayExtrasName.text=len
--const REPLAY_EXTRAS_ --const REPLAY_LINK_STYLE_
